<title>BRAZIL: Bunge International appoints new CEO.</title>
<headline>Bunge International appoints new CEO.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>South American food conglomerate Bunge International said it had appointed Oscar de Paula Bernardes Neto as its new chief executive officer.</p>
<p>Bernardes succeeds Ludwig Schmitt-Rhaden who has been elected chairman of the board, Bunge International said in a statement.</p>
<p>Former chairman Octavio Caraballo will continue as vice-chairman of the board, it said.</p>
<p>Bunge International said it had sales of $10 billion and had refocused its activities on the food and agribusiness sectors, mainly in North and South America, Australia and Asia.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
